# Line endings and merge strategy for the normalised taxonomy package.
#
# Measured before this file existed: two branches each adding one source conflicted on
# data/taxon.tsv, data/identifier.tsv and data/datapackage.json. Only the per-source mapping file
# merged cleanly, which is exactly what the design panel reported for every candidate design.
#
# `merge=union` keeps the lines from BOTH sides of a conflicted region instead of stopping. That is
# the right resolution for these three files and only these three: each is an append-only ledger of
# independent rows, so "both" is always the answer a curator would have typed. It is the WRONG
# strategy for a file where two edits can contradict each other, so nothing else gets it.
#
# Union merge is not free — it can leave the result unsorted, and it will happily keep two rows that
# claim the same id. Both are caught rather than hoped away: the validator's primary_key and
# unique_key rules fail on a duplicate id or a duplicate (name, rank, parent), and the canonical
# sort is restored by `fmt` (step 6). Until `fmt` exists, an out-of-order ledger is cosmetic; a
# duplicate id is a failing check.
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/taxonomy/data/taxon.tsv        merge=union
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/taxonomy/data/identifier.tsv   merge=union
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/taxonomy/data/merged.tsv       merge=union

# The package is canonical LF, no quoting, tab-separated. Declaring the files as text with `eol=lf`
# stops a Windows checkout from rewriting them to CRLF, which would break every byte comparison the
# golden gate makes — including the one against the published CSV.
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/taxonomy/data/**/*.tsv  text eol=lf
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/taxonomy/data/*.tsv     text eol=lf
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/taxonomy/data/*.json    text eol=lf

# The published wide CSV is byte-frozen: its first 1486 lines are pinned by a sha256 that a CRLF
# rewrite would invalidate on checkout, before anyone edited anything.
planktonzilla/planktonzilla_dataset/planktonzilla_taxonomy.csv  text eol=lf
